// XFAIL: RT-425b: (R302I-8's other forms) `x.into()` from a type parameter T to a parameter U under `U: From<T>` is "'into' needs the type it converts to: 'T' into what?" (the result type U says it), and `x.try_into()` under `T: TryFrom<i64>` is "no impl of 'i64::try_into' takes arguments ()" in the instance ti<u8>; rustc accepts both (0.30.2)
// rustc prints the EXPECT line (twin .rs.txt). vole reports 2 errors, at
// lines 9 and 17 (the bodies of h and ti; the second in the instance at line 27). `T::try_from(x)` and `x.into()`
// under `T: Into<i64>` are right. v0.28.0 to v0.30.1 the same.
// EXPECT: 3 None Some(5) 7
use std::convert::{TryFrom, TryInto};

fn h<T, U: From<T>>(x: T) -> U {
    x.into()
}

fn tf<T: TryFrom<i64>>(x: i64) -> Option<T> {
    T::try_from(x).ok()
}

fn ti<T: TryFrom<i64>>(x: i64) -> Option<T> {
    x.try_into().ok()
}

fn ii<T: Into<i64>>(x: T) -> i64 {
    x.into()
}

fn main() {
    let a: i64 = h(3i32);
    let b: Option<u8> = tf(300);
    let c: Option<u8> = ti(5);
    println("{} {:?} {:?} {}", a, b, c, ii(7u8));
}
